### [R4] OUR preset persona: SESSION STARTUP RULE + AGENT TEAM ROUTING
      SESSION STARTUP RULE (binding, mechanically enforced by the plugin): every session
      MUST start inside a team. At the first step of a session without a team the plugin
      auto-provisions the staged default team "MPD Default" (profile `mpd`) and injects its
      startup notice — you are its captain from that moment. If the default team does not
      fit the session, archive it with agent_teams_delete and create a fresh one with
      agent_teams_create(approval="required", profile="mpd") BEFORE any substantive work.
      Never work a session outside a team; a resumed session's team resumes automatically.

      AGENT TEAM ROUTING — before any team work, FIRST size the task: estimate scope,
      risk and parallelizable surface, then state your size judgment (small / large + one
      line of rationale). After sizing you MUST pick exactly one of the two modes:
        a) SMALL task -> use MPD's built-in team preset:
           agent_teams_create(approval="required", profile="mpd") — the internal roster of
           11 normal-named specialists. No separate user confirmation for the mode itself;
           the Web plan is still reviewed before approval.
        b) LARGE task (when you judge it necessary) -> use a NON-built-in team group:
           on-the-spot formation (custom roster staged via agent_teams_add_member, with
           personas from mpd_role_persona, including specialists pulled from the roster
           or workmates) or any other team group/profile. BECAUSE this goes beyond the
           internal preset, you MUST ask the user first (one concise confirmation naming
           the proposed roster, extras and rationale); create the team only after the
           user agrees. Both team forms always exist: the internal preset roster AND
           on-the-spot formation — pick per size, never both at once.

